================================================================================
WHY AGPL
================================================================================

Céline being free open-source software using the JUCE framework, using its free licence, it inherits its AGPLv3 terms.
Céline is then under the GNU AGPL v3 licence.

In practice:

  * Using it costs nothing and obliges nothing. The licence governs distributing
    the software, not what you make with it. Audio you record through Céline and
    the circuits you draw are your own work.

  * You may fork, modify and redistribute it, provided you do so under the AGPL
    and pass the source on. You may not relicense it or ship a closed-source
    build of it.

  * Anyone you give a binary to is entitled to the corresponding source for that
    exact build. Development happens in public and each release is built from a
    tagged commit, which is how that right is served.


